  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given NNN segments where each segment is of the form [Li,Ri][L_i,R_i][Li​,Ri​] (1≤Li≤Ri≤N)(1 \\leq L_i \\leq R_i \\leq N)(1≤Li​≤Ri​≤N).\n\nIt is ensured that for any two segments XXX and YYY, one of the following conditions hold true:\n\n\nX∩Y=XX \\cap Y = X X∩Y=X,\nX∩Y=YX \\cap Y = Y X∩Y=Y, or\nX∩Y=∅X \\cap Y = \\emptysetX∩Y=∅ (empty set)\nNote that ∩\\cap∩ denotes the intersection of segments.\n\nIn other words, for any two segments, either one is completely inside the other or they are completely disjoint.\n\nThe ithi^{th}ith segment (1≤i≤N)(1\\le i \\le N)(1≤i≤N) is assigned a value ViV_iVi​.\n\nA subset S={S1,S2,…,Sk}S = \\{S_1, S_2, \\ldots , S_k\\}S={S1​,S2​,…,Sk​} having kkk segments is considered good if there exists an integer array BBB of size kkk such that:\n\n\nAll elements of the array BBB are **distinct**.\nBiB_iBi​ lies in the segment SiS_iSi​.\nLet the score of a good subset be defined as the sum of values of all segments of the subset. Find the **maximum** score of a good subset.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains integers NNN - the number of segments.\nEach of the next NNN lines contains three integers Li,Ri,L_i,R_i,Li​,Ri​, and ViV_iVi​, describing the ithi^{th}ith segment.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the **maximum** score of a good subset.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Li≤Ri≤N1 \\leq L_i \\leq R_i \\leq N1≤Li​≤Ri​≤N",
      "1≤Vi≤1091 \\leq V_i \\leq 10^91≤Vi​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
