        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: A possible value of good subset is S=[A2,A4]S = [A_2, A_4]S=[A2​,A4​]. The array B=[2,3]B = [2, 3]B=[2,3] such that 222 lies in the segment A2A_2A2​ and 333 lies in the segment A4A_4A4​. The sum of values of all segments of SSS is 10+20=3010+20 = 3010+20=30.\nIt can be proven that the score of a good subset does not exceed 303030 in this case.\nTest case 222: We can take S=[A1,A2,A3,A4]S = [A_1, A_2, A_3, A_4]S=[A1​,A2​,A3​,A4​].\nThe array B=[2,3,1,4]B = [2, 3, 1, 4]B=[2,3,1,4].\n\nFor segment A1A_1A1​, L=1L = 1L=1 and R=3R = 3R=3. Here L1≤2≤R1L_1 \\le 2 \\le R_1L1​≤2≤R1​.\nFor segment A2A_2A2​, L=2L = 2L=2 and R=3R = 3R=3. Here L2≤3≤R2L_2 \\le 3 \\le R_2L2​≤3≤R2​.\nFor segment A3A_3A3​, L=1L = 1L=1 and R=1R = 1R=1. Here L3≤1≤R3L_3 \\le 1 \\le R_3L3​≤1≤R3​.\nFor segment A4A_4A4​, L=1L = 1L=1 and R=4R = 4R=4. Here L4≤4≤R4L_4 \\le 4 \\le R_4L4​≤4≤R4​.\n\nThe sum of scores of all segments of SSS is 4+5+10+13=324+5+10+13 = 324+5+10+13=32. It can be proven that the score of a good subset does not exceed 4+5+10+13=324+5+10+13=324+5+10+13=32 in this case."
